{
  "schema": "benchmark-v2-forward-cases-v1",
  "meta": {
    "purpose": "Curated forward gold set for cross-type ranking (Stage 0)",
    "provenance": "Authored from widely published open references. Deliberately carries NO expected_gers_id: an id could only have come from the system under test, which is what makes self-recall a retrievability claim rather than a quality one. Not derived from Nominatim or Photon either, so it stays usable for provider-neutral comparison.",
    "strata": {
      "seam": "query is simultaneously a division name and a POI context token; the division must win rank 1",
      "inverse_seam": "a POI must beat any same-named or homonym division",
      "name": "context-free global landmark retrieval (the known open gap)",
      "name_locality": "same landmark with a locality token; the control that should already pass",
      "named_poi": "an ordinary named restaurant, shop, hotel, hospital, library, or station with a locality token",
      "brand_branch": "a multi-location brand query that names the intended branch or neighborhood"
    },
    "limitations": [
      "55 cases is a seam and regression instrument, NOT the balanced multilingual gold set: coverage is Latin-script and Europe/North-America heavy.",
      "Coordinates are approximate landmark/city centroids with deliberately loose tolerances (25 km localities, 2 km POIs); this set scores type composition and retrieval, not positional accuracy.",
      "Overture may legitimately hold a place under a local-language primary name; alt_names cover the common cases but a miss should be inspected before it is called a regression.",
      "Generic category-intent queries such as 'restaurants near me' need relevance judgments and an explicit search origin, so they belong in a separate semantic benchmark rather than this exact-place gold set."
    ]
  },
